// gen-strip-goldens.mjs: what Node 24.18.0's module.stripTypeScriptTypes,
// in its default strip mode, makes of TypeScript sources, for lowering's
// stripTypes (strip.go): the lines an uncaught error's report quotes, since
// Node runs a .ts file as its stripped text (M6 plan D6).
//
//   node lower/testdata/gen-strip-goldens.mjs
//
// writes strip-goldens.jsonl beside this file, a line per source:
//   {"section":..., "name":..., "src":..., "lines":[...]}
// where lines is Node's output split as V8 numbers lines for an error's
// place, at \r\n, \n, \r, U+2028 and U+2029 (measured: a throw after each
// is reported on the line after it, and after U+0085, VT or FF on the same
// one). A source Node refuses has "refused":"<code>: <message>" in its
// place. Deterministic: nothing in a source or in what Node makes of it
// varies between runs.
//
// The sections hold the rules, each measured here first: one per kind of
// syntax, REFUSED for what Node refuses and stripTypes refuses too, and
// TS_ERRORS for sources Node refuses or strips otherwise for a reason
// TypeScript reports as an error itself, so lowering never strips them (the
// Go test holds each to that, not to Node's output). Then EXAMPLES,
// CAKEC_TESTS and UNCAUGHT: every .ts file in examples/, every program
// cmd/cakec's tests build, and every program of the runtime's uncaught
// goldens (backend/runtime/testdata/uncaught/), which this lists by running
//   go test ./lower -run TestStripGoldensHoldTheTestPrograms -args -strip-programs-out=<file>
// (strip_programs_test.go), the test that fails when one isn't here.

